/data/vm/vm-bake/distfiles
# @summary The directory of everything a bake fetches from outside, under VM_BAKE_DIR as distfiles is in FreeBSD: VM_BAKE_IMAGE_CACHE (image/) and VM_BAKE_PKG_DIR (pkg/) lie in it, and the bake hangs it onto /var/cache/pkg of the image for its run (image cache mount: nullfs on the host, the virtio-9p share distfiles in the builder), so pkg keeps every package it fetches here in its own layout and a bake that breaks off or is dropped costs no package twice; 'image pkg install' runs no pkg clean any more. Decided 31.10.2026 (same cache as the host), built 14.11. after three bakes had fetched texlive-docs from zero each.
